/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:35:  // krun. Python's float `%` is floor-based: a % b = a - floor(a/b)*b (K's %Float is IEEE
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:36:  // remainder, which differs — 3.5 %Float 1.0 = -0.5 vs Python 0.5 — so it is NOT used).
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:37:  syntax Float ::= floatMod(Float, Float) [function, total, symbol(floatMod), no-evaluators]
