codex
The root cause is now concrete: this sandbox exposes `/proc/self` using the host PID while processes see a different namespace PID (`$$` was 2), and Lean 4.22’s application-path lookup consequently cannot find `/proc/<namespace-pid>/exe`. I’m applying a narrow, auditable `/tmp` preload shim that maps `getpid()` to the host-visible `/proc/self` PID. It changes no K, Stage 3, Stage 4, or Lean project file; its only purpose is to let the pinned Lean executable locate itself. I’ll test `lean --version` before rerunning the required preflight.
